# This repo is PUBLIC (deploys to jwhwang91.github.io). Keep job-application
# artifacts out of git so the companies you apply to and your tailored resumes
# stay private.

# Each job application is one private folder here — jd.txt, overlay.yaml, notes.md,
# result.md, plus the generated resume.html and any PDF/evidence. The whole tree
# stays out of git (companies you apply to + tailored resumes are private).
/Applications/

# Flat Context/variants/*.yaml lenses (e.g. a reusable field focus like
# adas-controls.yaml) are NOT ignored and may be committed if you want them public.

# Private job-search constraints (work authorization / visa sponsorship, target
# list). Source of truth for the loop + rejection pipeline; must stay out of the
# public repo and is never rendered onto the resume.
/Context/candidate_profile.yaml

# Private working notes / session summaries — scratch space, not part of the
# published method. Keep out of the public repo.
/_session_notes/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# --- Phase 0 privacy hardening (this repo is PUBLIC) ---
# Raw source material for the portfolio (internal-looking decks, prior-employer
# photos, past PDFs). Untracked from HEAD; must never be re-committed.
/_source_references/

# Generated site output. CI (deploy.yml) rebuilds dist/ from scratch, so it must
# never be committed — committing it doubles the exposure surface and drifts from
# what is actually served.
/dist/

# Private side of the truth layer: phone/contact data, keyword-support cache
# (enumerates skill gaps), never-print redlines. Public repo — keep out.
/Context/private/

# JetBrains IDE project files — local tooling noise.
.idea/

# Tracker exports / ledger drafts that chart the job search. (The /Applications/
# rule above already covers these, but they are named explicitly for clarity.)
Applications/_track.csv
Applications/_ledger_draft.md

# macOS Finder noise.
.DS_Store

# local machine-specific double-click launcher (generated by `main.py ui`)
run-jobops.command

# owner-private job-search board data (served locally by the Discover screen)
ui/data/roles.json
